{"title":"2004 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Fryer Foundation is giving out four types of prizes, valued at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2668276d1c41b9274742bfcc30aef16cee0265bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbe8755ab50447cac8dac1ef464e9d4034f110d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b3e77d1e87399df4a1c08041805a142a9cb266c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b8219ded5e12beeb3c41192896b9fd564e3f692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are two ways in which the Foundation could give away prizes totalling <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bacecee55673f274c70223710dc81c364af119e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$880$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> while making sure to give away at least one and at most six of each prize. Determine the two ways of doing this, and explain how you got your answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a\" title=\"2004 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a\">solution 1 of part a</a>, we can realize that the value given for the prizes must be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a2dd6983f3fc5632ef1ae72d0a41649e4ce221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$780$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> for four of the prizes. Thus, the total value of the rest of the prizes must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed374247ea42952e132d5c4b07d30ee73913fd23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$880 - \\$780 = \\$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Since this total is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b3e77d1e87399df4a1c08041805a142a9cb266c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, we can focus specificially on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbe8755ab50447cac8dac1ef464e9d4034f110d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2668276d1c41b9274742bfcc30aef16cee0265bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> prizes. First, we notice that if we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbe8755ab50447cac8dac1ef464e9d4034f110d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> prizes, we get exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6a1da7f18069a90481296d18af7ca979fe3854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, so this is one way of getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bacecee55673f274c70223710dc81c364af119e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$880$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> in total. Next, we can try having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbe8755ab50447cac8dac1ef464e9d4034f110d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> prizes, which will give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610749c9007e75a2c3ade0209fdcc2b16264876b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" />. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2668276d1c41b9274742bfcc30aef16cee0265bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> prizes must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af281c0c0878cf4ca0997c94ef3354b3fee9e652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$100 - \\$75 = \\$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"17\" /> in total, so there must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac20804ddf020af6d1d90f4628b0e01e53943a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{5} = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2668276d1c41b9274742bfcc30aef16cee0265bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> prizes. Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> since we had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of each prize already, we see that we meet the bounds of the problem.\n</p><p>Thus, to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bacecee55673f274c70223710dc81c364af119e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$880$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" />, we can have one of the following combinations of prizes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2668276d1c41b9274742bfcc30aef16cee0265bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> prize, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbe8755ab50447cac8dac1ef464e9d4034f110d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> prizes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b3e77d1e87399df4a1c08041805a142a9cb266c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> prize, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b8219ded5e12beeb3c41192896b9fd564e3f692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> prize\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2668276d1c41b9274742bfcc30aef16cee0265bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> prizes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbe8755ab50447cac8dac1ef464e9d4034f110d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> prizes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b3e77d1e87399df4a1c08041805a142a9cb266c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> prize, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b8219ded5e12beeb3c41192896b9fd564e3f692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> prize\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203759\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 132/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 287/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6977/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.870      1 2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    6.870      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36920:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017203759 and revision id 285717. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}